# R-baseline — the known-good reference config, restored, plus ONE justified delta.
#
# PROVENANCE
#   github.com/bumblebeers/dsv4-flash-2x-spark-deployment @ d4f9c48 (2026-09-14),
#   docs/STACK029.md "Recommended serving profile" -> profiles/K-ours-opt.env.
#   Every serving value below is the reference's, verbatim. Deviations must carry their
#   own justification in this header; that is the point of this file.
#
# JUSTIFIED DELTA (1 of 1) — vision mm-prefix-span fix
#   Measured 2026-09-23 with scripts/dsv4-coord-probe.py, slope of predicted-vs-true y.
#   With the V2 model runner, compute_mm_prefix_ranges derives mm-prefix bidirectional
#   ranges from PlaceholderRange.extract_embeds_range() instead of the full sentinel block,
#   so image rows leak into causal attention and predicted y collapses to the image centre.
#     before: y-slope 0.287, y mean abs err 19.09% (146.6 px); y pinned at 50.0
#     after:  y-slope 0.981 (r 0.999), y mean abs err 0.79% (6.1 px)
#   BOTH HALVES ARE REQUIRED. The overlay reads the two flags via getattr(..., 0/False) and
#   silently takes the UNFIXED branch when they are absent from the checkpoint config.json
#   — which they are. So MMPREFIX_FIX=1 alone would be a no-op without EXTRA_ARGS.
#
# NOT DELTAS — deliberately restored reference values, with what they replace:
#   GPU_UTIL=0.88   (was 0.85)  reference value; 0.85 was a margin added on top of the
#                               baseline after the 2026-09-24 freeze investigation
#   MAX_NUM_SEQS=16 (was 12)    reference value; 12 rested on MiaAI #141 evidence that was
#                               never reproduced on this image (the 64-row FlashInfer
#                               dispatch boundary is real — _DECODE_MAX_TOKENS — but the
#                               hazard is inherited). Worth ~+403k tokens if it holds
#   MAX_BATCHED=2048 (was 2304) reference value
#   LPT=unset       (was 2048)  reference value; the fairness reserve was a tuning choice
#                               that costs pool
#
# EXTRA_ENV is pinned EXPLICITLY rather than left to the launcher: expandable_segments:True
# is PyTorch's and eugr's default and is what the reference ran (its EXTRA_ENV was empty).
# Pinning it here means an upstream default change cannot silently move it. False was
# adopted 2026-09-23 for +616,169 tokens of pool and is the more fragmentation-prone mode —
# i.e. it trades away the mechanism that mitigates the prefill high-water mark.
GPU_UTIL=0.88; MAX_NUM_SEQS=16; MAX_BATCHED=2048; CAPTURE_SIZES="[1,2,4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,36,40,44,48,52,56,60,64]"
K=3; DRAFT_METHOD=probabilistic; EFFORT=high; LIMIT_IMAGES=8
RETENTION=4096; FORCE_A16=1; OVERRIDE_GEN='{"temperature":1.0,"top_p":0.95}'; PARSER_FIX=1; OPROJ=overlay; EP=0
EXTRA_ENV="PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True"
MMPREFIX_FIX=1
EXTRA_ARGS="--hf-overrides '{\"mm_prefix_span_leading_pad_modulus\":4,\"mm_prefix_clamp_sliding_window\":true}'"
